.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_MD-BLAKE2 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_MD-BLAKE2
.Nd The BLAKE2 EVP_MD implementation
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Support for computing BLAKE2 digests through the
.Sy EVP_MD
API.
.Ss Identities
This implementation is only available with the default provider, and
includes the following varieties:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It BLAKE2S-256
Known names are "BLAKE2S-256" and "BLAKE2s256".
.It BLAKE2B-512
Known names are "BLAKE2B-512" and "BLAKE2b512".
.El
.Ss Settable Parameters
"BLAKE2B-512" supports the following
.Xr EVP_MD_CTX_set_params 3
key described in
.Xr EVP_DigestInit 3 .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqsize" ( Ns Sy OSSL_DIGEST_PARAM_SIZE Ns ) <unsigned integer>
.El
.Ss Gettable Parameters
This implementation supports the common gettable parameters described in
.Xr EVP_MD-common 7 .
.Ss Settable Context Parameters
The implementation supports the following
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
entries which are settable for an
.Sy EVP_MD_CTX
with
.Xr EVP_DigestInit_ex2 3
or
.Xr EVP_MD_CTX_set_params 3 :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqsize" ( Ns Sy OSSL_DIGEST_PARAM_SIZE Ns ) <unsigned integer>
Sets a different digest length for the
.Xr EVP_DigestFinal 3
output.
The value of the "size" parameter must not exceed the default digest
length of the respective BLAKE2 algorithm variants, 64 for BLAKE2B-512
and 32 for BLAKE2S-256. The parameter must be set with the
.Xr EVP_DigestInit_ex2 3
call to have an immediate effect.
When set with
.Xr EVP_MD_CTX_set_params 3
it will have an effect only if the
.Sy EVP_MD_CTX
context is reinitialized.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr provider-digest 7 ,
.Xr OSSL_PROVIDER-default 7
.Sh HISTORY
This functionality was added in OpenSSL 3.0.
.Pp
The variable size support was added in OpenSSL 3.2 for BLAKE2B-512 and
in OpenSSL 3.3 for BLAKE2S-256.
